WEBVTT

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:09.210
There once was a war.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.930
A conflict that arose from a single colony's independence movement...

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:23.810
...grew into an all-out war that engulfed the entire Earth.

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:30.400
Eight months after the fighting reached a stalemate,

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:34.570
the Space Revolutionary Army demanded the surrender of the United Nations Earth,

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.030
threatening to launch a colony drop operation...

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:40.620
...that would inflict catastrophic damage on the Earth.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:46.040
In response, the United Nations Earth Forces sent in their ultimate secret weapon,

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.580
the Mobile Suit Gundam,

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:51.090
and prepared to fight to the bitter end.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:33.300
However, this one volley proved to be the trigger...

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.970
...for the greatest tragedy in human history.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.470
Eager for victory, the S.R.A. went through with their operation.

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:45.140
The U.N.E.F. held their ground and fought back.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:47.890
The fighting became bogged down,

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:51.900
and in the end, catastrophic damage was dealt...

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:55.070
...to the Earth, the home of all mankind.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:59.530
Most of humanity, which had been 10 billion strong, was lost.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:03.370
Victory and defeat became a moot point in this war.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:15.170
And then, 15 years passed...

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:25.060
<b>After War</b>

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:25.060
<b>GUNDAM</b>

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:32.560
<b>The dream I'd nearly forgotten is beginning to stir,</b>

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.530
<b>little by little</b>

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:40.070
<b>filling in the gaps in my heart.</b>

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:47.450
<b>The instant my frozen memories begin to awaken,</b>

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:56.960
<b>my only wish is for the future that is about to begin.</b>

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:00.760
<b>I'll reach out with both hands</b>

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:04.510
<b>and embrace that dream I once had</b>

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:08.140
<b>I want to go on believing</b>

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:12.060
<b>without ever letting go or giving up</b>

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:15.690
<b>Until the day comes when I grab hold...</b>

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:19.570
<b>...of that dream I once had,</b>

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:23.110
<b>I want to keep chasing after it</b>

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:29.000
<b>without ever forgetting my hopes and dreams</b>

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:39.460
<b>Episode 1</b>

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:39.460
<b>"Is the Moon Out?"</b>

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.510
The colony drop had a profound effect on the Earth.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:53.060
There was environmental upheaval and ecosystem destruction,

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:57.440
and there was no rest for the handful of humans who lived through it.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.400
However, in spite of everything, the human race survived.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:05.200
Or rather, they had to survive.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:07.950
After War 15.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:11.500
The Earth's environment had finally entered a period of stability.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:17.170
People try to survive today in hopes of better times to come.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:26.140
Always a pleasure!

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:29.260
I'm running a special sale today!

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:33.390
Step right up!

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:36.150
Step right up, step right up!

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:43.360
I'm sure that you've all heard the rumors...

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:46.200
...about soldiers with superpowers in the war!

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:51.160
But when people say these are wild stories or tall tales, they are wrong!

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:55.580
In fact, this man is a surviving member of those super-soldiers!

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:01.590
He must be, considering that he and I destroyed 15 ships in the great battle!

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:05.090
We were known far and wide as the Red Bi-stars!

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:10.640
I represent the evolved humanity that was to usher in the space age.

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:16.020
In these turbulent times, our powers are needed more than ever!

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:20.360
What do you say? Hire us now while you can!

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:23.360
Oh, come on! That was just a job pitch?!

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:28.490
Hey! We might not look like much, but when push comes to shove, we-

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:32.540
It's a mobile suit!

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:39.880
Looks like I'm in for a good haul today!

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.380
Damn it, it's a bandit!

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:51.260
Hey, it's not like I'm trying to kill everybody!

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:54.390
But if that's how you want it, I'll take off the kiddy gloves!

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:02.320
Hey, Red Whatchamacallits! Do something, damn it!

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:10.990
No, dummy! I need armor-piercing!

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:18.870
Crap, the city was finally making progress!

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:22.540
People who can use mobile suits think they can do whatever they want!

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:27.090
I just need to hit the cockpit... Eat this!

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:30.380
Oh, no!

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:42.610
Wha-?

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:45.110
Catch!

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:59.160
Crap, my main camera!

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.710
Who the hell did that?!

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:04.130
I did!

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:08.300
This is what's called a stick-up.

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:11.590
Wh-Where did you come from?

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:14.050
Careful, now! No funny moves!

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:19.270
I bet I can fire this before your mobile suit can squash me.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:24.560
I like you, kid. If you want, I can make you my partner.

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:26.190
Get real.

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:29.570
Like I said, this is a stick-up.

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:32.610
Ow...

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:40.960
H-Help me!

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:44.380
That kid's got some moves.

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:49.800
Are you Garrod Ran?

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:52.050
I thought so!

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:56.100
My name is Rike Anto! I've been looking for you!

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:58.890
Is this about a job?

00:07:59.100 --> 00:07:59.970
Yes!

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:02.060
Come see me in a bit, then!

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:04.980
I need to sell this baby off first!

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:15.910
It's seems like a waste to sell off an undamaged mobile suit...

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:17.490
...to a traveling mecha dealer.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:20.830
It's not a waste at all. They're worth good money.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:23.790
I wasn't speaking of money.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:27.460
You have detailed knowledge of mobile suits.

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:30.670
I expect that you are also a fair pilot.

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:36.220
Thanks, but no thanks. Piloting a mobile suit is a good job,

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:38.760
but the downside is that people try to kill you.

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:43.390
Not surprising, since mobile suits are the biggest treasure left from the war.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:49.320
Pilots fight each other to try and take the other person's mobile suit, right?

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:53.320
Pilot one of those things, and you'll need way more than nine lives.

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:55.150
Besides...

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:00.280
Anyway, let's talk business!

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:01.620
Very well.

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:09.210
I won't go into detail as to why.

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:12.090
If you ask, no answers will be forthcoming.

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:15.880
Word of your abilities is what led me to seek you out.

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:21.060
The girl's name is Tiffa Adill. I want you to rescue her.

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:23.270
Rescue her?

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:27.440
She has been abducted by a Vulture.

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:31.570
A vulture is a carrion-eating bird.

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:35.440
But in this era, Vulture has a second meaning.

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:38.780
There are those who scavenge the ruins of old...

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:41.780
...military installations for remains of weapons and electronics...

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:43.990
...and sell them to anyone with the money.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:48.960
People call them Vultures after the carrion-eating birds.

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:52.920
Looks like we've lost our pursuers.

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:56.050
Keep an eye on things.

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:56.920
Yes, sir.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:05.180
We sure went to a lot of trouble to nab one little girl.

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:08.100
I wonder what the Captain wants her for?

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:09.310
Beats me.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:21.550
We're ready over here! Fire up the pump!

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:22.760
On it!

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:27.260
Make it snappy! At this rate, we won't reach St. Lange before morning!

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:44.030
Oh, come on! Aren't you done pumping that water yet?!

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:47.990
I'm in the middle of a shower, so hurry it up! Sheesh!

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:52.750
I almost saw some goodies...

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:55.290
Right! Speaking of goodies!

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:24.820
These guys are Vultures, so they're bound to have something valuable.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:28.410
Bingo!

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:33.290
What the heck is that?

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:39.040
A mobile suit's control unit?

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:42.090
What the heck. It's better than walking away empty-handed.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:48.050
We're moving out, so get ready!

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:48.760
Understood! Understood!

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:51.270
That's not good. I need to hurry.

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:39.560
Excuse me...

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:44.990
Um... I'm here to... Uh...

00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:50.200
N-No, not that! Hang on, not what?

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:52.450
Aw, what the heck am I saying?!

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:54.750
Look, I mean...

00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:00.250
Oh! I'm here to rescue you!

00:14:11.260 --> 00:14:14.390
I mean it. I'm here to rescue you.

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:27.570
I've... been waiting for you.

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:38.790
Main engine activated! Freeden, now launching!

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:41.790
Hold on! Hatch #4 is still open!

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:50.590
Heat sources closing in from 8 o'clock!

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:56.430
Mobile suits!

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:58.350
Freeden, emergency liftoff!

00:14:58.390 --> 00:14:59.060
Yes, sir!

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:07.070
Vultures fighting Vultures?

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:09.820
Well, it's perfect timing for us!

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:11.950
Hold on tight!

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:26.630
I knew I could count on you. You're right on time.

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:29.590
A job's a job.

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:31.470
Okay, Tiffa.

00:15:34.430 --> 00:15:36.010
What's the matter?

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:41.770
All right, Tiffa... Come to me.

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:46.360
Hey, what's the matter?

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:49.820
What are you waiting? Come to me.

00:15:50.070 --> 00:15:51.780
No!

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:55.370
Get out of the buggy now!

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:01.710
Come back here!

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:05.960
Is this what you want, Tiffa?

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:11.300
What the heck! We'll just play it by ear!

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:18.390
This is an emergency! Contact the main office and send mobile suits!

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:21.890
What? The Vultures? Ignore them!

00:16:22.390 --> 00:16:23.560
Yes, immediately!

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:28.320
You're sure this is the right way?

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:31.070
Is there a house up ahead?

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:33.240
What, then?

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:35.860
A very important power.

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:42.450
What the...?

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:48.340
I think we're in serious trouble here!

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:50.420
Keep going straight ahead.

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:52.800
Go straight!

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:54.760
I don't think that's a good idea!

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:57.470
It missed!

00:16:58.180 --> 00:16:59.050
Go left!

00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:03.680
Go right!

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:11.900
Damn, I can't believe we couldn't slow down a little buggy!

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:15.530
It's not working, we have to actually try to hit them.

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:16.610
Go around!

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:17.700
Yes, sir! Yes, sir!

00:17:18.070 --> 00:17:21.160
Wow, what the heck is going on?

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:25.410
Oh, right... Maybe everybody is after that "power" she mentioned.

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:31.550
What's that?

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:32.800
Go inside.

00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:34.260
If you say so.

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:35.470
Right!

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:42.140
You won't get me that easily!

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:51.980
Damn.

00:17:52.070 --> 00:17:54.320
It looks like the ruins of an old U.N.E. factory.

00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:56.190
Orders, Director?

00:17:56.740 --> 00:18:00.490
Our objective is Tiffa. Keep after them!

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:05.660
Have they given up?

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:08.170
What is this place, anyway?

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:10.290
A mobile suit factory?

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:32.940
Tiffa!

00:18:44.030 --> 00:18:46.160
Th-That's a...

00:18:47.290 --> 00:18:49.660
A Gundam?

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:53.460
Tiffa!

00:18:55.750 --> 00:18:57.590
Tiffa! Tiffa!

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:02.090
Damn it...

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:04.050
If that works, maybe I can...

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:05.810
I may as well try!

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:13.690
That's... the GX-9900!

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:19.530
Please work!

00:19:19.570 --> 00:19:20.530
What?!

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:22.410
The joystick's missing!

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:32.420
I can't believe that thing's armor! It's not even scratched!

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:36.170
It's not operational. Grab onto it and pry open the cockpit.

00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:37.340
Yes, sir! Yes, sir!

00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:41.380
If this works, sign me up as a believer in God!

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:42.470
Here goes!

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:45.680
It worked!

00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:51.480
Tiffa! I believe in God!

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:55.190
Okay, let's do this!

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:00.690
Impossible!

00:20:01.030 --> 00:20:03.200
On your feet, damn it!

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:12.500
You've had your fun, chasing us all over the place!

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:13.620
Eat this!

00:20:27.300 --> 00:20:28.390
Fall back!

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:29.390
Y-Yes, sir!

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:31.520
Come back here!

00:20:54.370 --> 00:20:55.500
Did we get it?

00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:05.680
What?!

00:21:31.740 --> 00:21:33.870
We're safe now, Tiffa.

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:37.080
What's the matter, Tiffa?

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:48.800
A Gundam-type, huh? I'm dying to take this one on.

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:52.560
Good grief. Fine, be my guest.

00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:55.560
Gundams? Two of them?

00:22:04.530 --> 00:22:05.860
Is the Moon out?

00:22:07.600 --> 00:22:10.200
I asked you if the Moon is out!

00:22:45.690 --> 00:22:50.990
<b>Can I find the words to tell you</b>

00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:52.410
Garrod, who has obtained the Gundam X to protect Tiffa,

00:22:51.070 --> 00:22:56.370
<b>How I live between the walls of steel and stone</b>

00:22:52.410 --> 00:22:57.410
is confronted by two Gundams, as well as the Vultures who have pursued them.

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:00.290
A horde of mobile suits bear down on them.

00:22:58.040 --> 00:23:04.210
<b>How I close my eyes to find some kind of rapture</b>

00:23:00.290 --> 00:23:04.290
In the end, Tiffa activates a forbidden system.

00:23:04.930 --> 00:23:10.570
<b>In a world where you can feel so all alone</b>

00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:17.550
<b>Inside I'm full of light and laughter</b>

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:21.440
<b>There's a flame that burns in me</b>

00:23:21.440 --> 00:23:22.420
<b>(I need a way)</b>

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:26.480
<b>(I need a way) I need a way to set it free</b>

00:23:26.480 --> 00:23:31.400
<b>When you find love in your heart</b>

00:23:31.400 --> 00:23:33.530
<b>(The human touch)</b>

00:23:33.530 --> 00:23:37.590
<b>You can believe from the start</b>

00:23:37.590 --> 00:23:39.580
<b>(From the start)</b>

00:23:40.510 --> 00:23:42.710
<b>Dreams they come true</b>

00:23:42.710 --> 00:23:44.080
<b>(They come true)</b>

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:48.420
<b>All comes to you, oh all at once</b>

00:23:48.420 --> 00:23:52.240
<b>If you believe in human touch</b>

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:53.890
I will give you power.

00:23:53.970 --> 00:23:56.600
<b>Episode 2</b>

00:23:53.970 --> 00:23:56.600
<b>"I Will Give You Power"</b>

00:23:56.600 --> 00:23:58.600
<b></b>
